$ cc-share announce on
avahi-daemon isn't running, so the Frame can't find this machine. Run cc-share fix --announce (or sudo systemctl enable --now avahi-daemon), then this again.
[exit 1]
$ cc-share fix --announce --yes
avahi: to start avahi-daemon now and at every boot, because the Frame lists this machine through it:
+ sudo systemctl enable --now avahi-daemon
avahi: avahi-daemon is running and starts at boot
avahi: to turn publishing on in HOME/avahi-daemon.conf (only disable-publishing and disable-user-service-publishing in [publish]; the original is kept as HOME/avahi-daemon.conf.before-command-center):
+ sudo cp -p HOME/avahi-daemon.conf HOME/avahi-daemon.conf.before-command-center
+ sudo install -m 644 HOME/.config/control-center/avahi-daemon.conf.new HOME/avahi-daemon.conf
+ sudo systemctl restart avahi-daemon
avahi: publishing is on, and avahi-daemon restarted. The original is in HOME/avahi-daemon.conf.before-command-center; cc-install --remove puts it back
[exit 0]
